00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.650
There aren't any consistency
challenges the way

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.710
you might see with other
cloud storage offerings

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:09.919
from other cloud providers.

00:02:09.919 --> 00:02:12.650
Geo-redundancy-- so
all of Cloud Storage

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:16.020
is built around a global
approach to storage.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.770
So we have regions, dual
regions, multi-regions.

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.270
And we make it very
easy to actually

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:24.985
have your storage distributed
with geo-redundancy.

00:02:24.985 --> 00:02:26.360
And then finally,
of course, what

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:28.970
you would expect from
Cloud-- scalability,

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:31.130
no matter whether
you need gigabytes,

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:35.740
terabytes, petabytes,
or exabytes of storage.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.290
So this is all
made possible based

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.630
on the enormous
investments that Google has

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:42.150
made in core infrastructure.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:48.225
So this, of course, started long
before GCP actually existed.

00:02:48.225 --> 00:02:50.100
This infrastructure was
